### 11. ALIGNMENT & VISUAL HIERARCHY

This is one of the highest-priority requirements.

Follow professional graphic-design alignment principles.

Rules:

1. All page headings must follow consistent horizontal alignment.
2. All content panels must follow the same grid system.
3. Related labels and values must have consistent alignment.
4. Cards within the same group must share consistent spacing.
5. Text alignment must reflect the information hierarchy.
6. Metadata must remain visually secondary.
7. Numerical information must have clear visual priority.
8. Section headings must align with their corresponding content.
9. Buttons must align logically with the component they control.
10. Avoid arbitrary positioning and inconsistent margins.

Never fix alignment issues by introducing random padding values.

Use shared layout tokens and reusable grid structures.

